{
  "name": "Modular Tools",
  "icon": "draconicevolution:draconic_pickaxe",
  "category": "draconicevolution:equipment",
  "sortnum": 2,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Pickaxe, shovel, axe, hoe, sword and bow come in Wyvern, Draconic and Chaotic tiers. Each tier mines faster and hits harder than the last, but all of them depend on $(l:equipment/modules)modules$(/l) and stored energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Which modules fit depends on the tool: pickaxe and shovel take mining modules, the sword takes weapon modules, the axe takes both plus Tree Harvest, the hoe takes AOE, and the bow takes projectile modules."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "title": "Staff of Power",
      "text": "The $(item)Staff of Power$() (Draconic and Chaotic only) is a pickaxe, shovel, axe and sword in one, with a much bigger module grid. It is made from the matching pickaxe, shovel and sword.$(br2)Tool Config ($(l)C$()) sets mining speed, AOE size and similar options, so a big AOE tool can still dig a single block."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "title": "Capacitors",
      "text": "A $(item)Capacitor$() is a portable battery. It stores nothing until you add energy modules. In Tool Config, choose what it charges: the held item, worn armour, the hotbar, the main inventory, and Curios slots when Curios is installed."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "title": "Recipes",
      "text": "Tools are made by $(l:fusion_crafting/overview)Fusion Crafting$(/l). The Wyvern tool uses the vanilla diamond tool as its catalyst; each higher tier uses the tier below. The pickaxe line is shown here; every other tool follows the same pattern, so look the rest up in JEI."
    },
    {
